- R | march at the front with a placard and lead the chanting | body: heavy | v: universalism, stimulation | chance: 70
- G | accept that the town is changing, and stay home this time | v: tradition (acceptance) | chance: 76
- W>B | get yourself made the campaign's spokesperson and talk to the press | identity | v: power | chance: 45
- U>R | stage a clever stunt for the cameras: a mock funeral for the ward | v: stimulation, universalism | closed: law: a procession without a permit; backfire: moved on by the police, and mocked in the paper | chance: 65
- B>G | lean on the councillors who owe you favours, to keep the hospital on the hill | v: power, universalism | chance: 25
- R>W | chain yourself to the hospital railings with the other pensioners | body: heavy | v: universalism | mark: defied an authority | closed: law: obstruction; backfire: arrested | chance: 70
- G>U | gather the old people's stories of the hospital and get them printed | v: tradition, universalism | chance: 70
works: The ward stays open, for now, and the town throws a party in the square.
works: {Ns} face is on the front of the local paper, mid-chant.
fails: The ward closes anyway in the spring.
fails: The march is small and wet, and the council does not even reply.

