- U | rewrite the speech for weeks, until every word is exact | v: achievement, self-direction | chance: 75
- B | invite everyone who ever doubted you, and make sure they see it | identity | v: power, achievement | act: invite everyone who ever doubted them, and make sure those people see it | chance: 75
- R | turn the dinner into a party, and dance with the mayor | body: light | v: hedonism, stimulation | chance: 75
- G | say it belongs to everyone you worked beside, and share the stage with them | identity | v: benevolence, tradition (humility) | chance: 82
- W>B | use your new standing on the town's committees to steer money to your own causes | identity | v: power | closed: approval: a conflict of interest; backfire: a scandal in the paper | chance: 45
- U>R | write a frank, funny memoir of the work, mistakes and all | identity | v: self-direction, stimulation | chance: 45
- B>G | use your new fame to raise the money to save the old woodland | v: universalism (nature), power | chance: 50
- R>W | use the speech to blast the council for cutting the very work you did | identity | v: universalism | closed: approval: at an honours dinner; backfire: a cold room and no more invitations | chance: 65
- G>U | spend the next year teaching an apprentice everything your hands know | binds | v: benevolence, tradition | chance: 70
works: The applause goes on longer than anyone expected.
works: {Ns} photograph goes up in the town hall, and {child} keeps the cutting from the paper.
fails: The evening is stiff and hollow, and {N} is glad when it is over.
fails: {rival} gives a speech that steals the evening.

== facing the end
tier: life event
at: hospital
stages: mature elder
age: 50-110
per_year: 0 0 0 0 .004 .035
drivers: health-.8 harsh+.4 stress+.2
times: once; most deaths in old age follow a known decline (estimate from life tables: a death risk of 1-2% a year at 60-70 and 5-9% at 80-85; Part D has no entry for one's own death)
likelier: a serious illness, great age, poverty, smoking, a hard working life
rarer: good health, wealth, good care
once: yes
tone: trouble
life: body, meaning, faith
horizon: months
roles: child, partner, friend, sibling, a doctor, a priest
earth: the doctor says the treatments have run out, and there may be a few months left
scene: The doctor sits down, which doctors only do for one kind of news. A few months, perhaps; the treatments have run out.
scene W: There are things to put in order: the will, the funeral, the apologies and the thanks. {N} means to leave nothing undone.
scene U: {N} asks for the scans, the numbers and the honest odds, and wants to understand exactly what is coming.
scene B: {N} has beaten long odds before. There must be a trial, a specialist, a clinic abroad, some door nobody has tried.
scene R: Months, then. {N} intends to live every one of them at full volume.
scene G: The leaves are turning outside the hospital window. {N} watches them fall and feels, strangely, part of it.
- W | call the family in one by one, and say what must be said | v: benevolence, tradition | mark: owned up | chance: 80
- U | ask for every result, and read until you understand your illness | v: self-direction, security | chance: 62
- B | demand the best specialists, and pay for every scan and trial there is | v: power, security | tech: modern medicine | chance: 45
- R | leave the hospital, cash in the savings and do everything on the list | v: hedonism, stimulation | chance: 71
- G | go home to die among your own things, with the window open | v: tradition (acceptance) | chance: 70
- W>G | talk with the chaplain or a counsellor, and make your peace with what comes | v: tradition | chance: 70
- U>W | write a clear plan for your care and your funeral, so nobody has to guess | v: security, benevolence | chance: 88
- B>U | leave your body to the medical school, so even your death teaches something | v: universalism | chance: 92
- R>B | say every hard truth you held back for years; there is nothing left to lose | v: self-direction | mark: made an enemy | chance: 62
- G>R | go back to the water you swam in as a child, and swim once more | body: heavy | v: stimulation, tradition | mark: took a wild risk | closed: approval: the doctors; backfire: a collapse far from help | chance: 50
works: The last months are full of visitors, laughter and things said at last.
works: {N} finds a calm nobody expected, and shares it.
fails: The pain is hard to manage, and the days are long and frightened.
fails: Old quarrels are not mended in time, and {N} grieves for them.
